 {"id":"6.1","q":"The tyre industry has three organised players and several unorganised players. About 20% of total sales come from the unorganised sector. The three major companies reported revenue of Rs 6,000 crore, Rs 8,000 crore and Rs 10,000 crore. Which is closest to a fair estimate of the overall market size?","o":["Rs 30,000 crore","Rs 48,000 crore","Rs 24,000 crore","Rs 36,000 crore"],"a":0,"w":"Book sample question. Organised = 24,000 = 80% of the market. 24,000 &divide; 0.8 = 30,000."},
 {"id":"6.2","q":"In an industry where rivalry is high, the end result will be ______ pricing power and ______ incomes for the industry participants.","o":["Lower; lower","Lower; higher","Higher; higher","Higher; lower"],"a":0,"w":"Book sample question."},
 {"id":"6.3","q":"Which of the following is considered an economic factor in PESTLE analysis?","o":["Forex reserves","Monetary policies of the RBI","Country's dependence on other countries for important natural resources","All of the above"],"a":3,"w":"Book sample question. All three are listed under economic factors."},
 {"id":"6.4","q":"Which of the following relates to industry structure in Structure Conduct Performance (SCP) analysis?","o":["Industry growth rate","Relationship among the various players in the industry","Market size","All of the above"],"a":3,"w":"Book sample question. Structure covers competitive intensity, concentration, relationships, market size and growth."},
 {"id":"6.5","q":"Financial services, comprising insurance, banking, credit rating and investment banking, is an example of a(n):","o":["Business sector","Industry","Economic sector","Sub-industry"],"a":0,"w":"A business sector groups related industries. Economic sectors are agriculture, manufacturing, utilities, services."},
