 {"id":"6.24","q":"In the Indian sugar industry, the price of sugarcane is decided by the government after considering farmers' views. This indicates:","o":["Strong bargaining power of suppliers","Strong bargaining power of buyers","High threat of substitutes","Low entry barriers"],"a":0,"w":"The input cost depends on what the suppliers demand."},
 {"id":"6.25","q":"Warren Buffett's \"economic castles protected by unbreachable moats\" refers to businesses with:","o":["High barriers to entry","High industry rivalry","Strong supplier power","Many substitutes"],"a":0,"w":"Moats keep new entrants out and give pricing power."},
 {"id":"6.26","q":"Which is NOT a feature of an attractive industry from the shareholders' perspective?","o":["Strong buyers' bargaining power","Low competition","High barriers to entry","Few substitutes"],"a":0,"w":"An attractive industry has weak buyer and supplier power."},
